<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.11.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02280</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.11.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>eecf22e1-984c-43db-8ec3-5505af6355bd</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_2cf37e70-fdd6-46dc-a766-bfd6dd4b69ef" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>For questions 1 – 4, identify a quadratic function in standard form, \(f(x)\), with the given zeros.</para>
            <para>1 and 9</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 10x + 9\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 8x + 9\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 8x + 9\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.11.2. 
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 − 10x + 9\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_07db76f5-fe1a-47b7-a8f4-d6338a20b858" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(\sqrt5\) and \(-\sqrt{5}\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 5x − 5\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 5x − 5\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 5\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 5\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.11.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 − 5\).

      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="ff482616-7944-4fc5-9ae2-3b54d7a076b0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>–7</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 14x + 49\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 14x − 49\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 49\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 14x + 49\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.11.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 + 14x + 49\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c0d873b5-60e8-4b43-9c28-d67fa7c53f36" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>–3</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 6x + 9\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 9\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 9\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 9\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.11.2. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 9\).
        </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4c636bc6-210b-4a8a-af32-6a02cfa78d9e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Examine the graph below to identify the zeros of the function. Then, write a quadratic function in standard form with the given zeros.</para>
            <figure>
              <media alt="A PARABOLA THAT OPENS UP WITH \(x\)-intercepts OF NEGATIVE 5 AND 1.">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_09_13_10_01.jpg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 4x − 5\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 6x − 5\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 4x − 5\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 6x − 5\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.11.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 + 4x − 5\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_52010894-9061-4963-87c8-7e33c014fee6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <newline/>
            <para>Examine the graph below to identify the zeros of the function. Then, write a quadratic function in standard form with the given zeros.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 2x − 8\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 − 6x + 8\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 2x − 8\)</para>
            <para>\(f(x) = x^2 + 6x + 8\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.11.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(f(x) = x^2 − 6x + 8\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_382279dc-b26c-458b-bbc8-215732e20d35" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the specific quadratic function, \(p(x)\), in standard form, that has the zeros –8 and 3 and passes through the point \((2, -20)\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(p(x) = 2x^2 + 10x − 48\)</para>
            <para>\(p(x) = 3x^2 + 15x − 72\)</para>
            <para>\(p(x) = −x^2 − 5x − 24\)</para>
            <para>\(p(x) = −x^2 − 5x − 6\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.11.3 and 8.11.4. 
      </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(p(x) = 2x^2 + 10x − 48\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d8bf81db-a6a2-4606-87d8-62d38118a5b4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the specific quadratic function, \(g(x)\), in standard form, that has the zero 2 and passes through the point \((3, -3)\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(g(x) = x^2 − 4x + 4\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x) = 2x^2 − 8x + 3\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x) = −2x^2 + 8x − 8\)</para>
            <para>\(g(x) = −3x^2 + 12x − 12\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.11.3 and 8.11.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(g(x) = −3x^2 + 12x − 12\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_432a5130-fca8-457c-ba48-e4760bd43c87" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the specific quadratic function, \(h(x)\), in standard form, that has the zeros 3 and 5 and passes through the point \((2, 12)\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(h(x) = x^2 − 8x + 15\)</para>
            <para>\(h(x) = 4x^2 − 32x + 60\)</para>
            <para>\(h(x) = −x^2 + 8x − 15\)</para>
            <para>\(h(x) = 3x^2 − 24x + 48\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.11.3 and 8.11.4. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(h(x) = 4x^2 − 32x + 60\).
      </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="edc67eae-edda-4a6b-80d1-0160b01d0141" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the specific quadratic function, \(w(x)\), in standard form, that has the zeros 6 and –7 and passes through the point \((5, 12)\).</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(w(x) = x^2 + x − 42\)</para>
            <para>\(w(x) = 2x^2 + 2x − 48\)</para>
            <para>\(w(x) = −2x^2 − 2x + 84\)</para>
            <para>\( w(x) = −x^2 − x + 42\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.11.3 and 8.11.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \( w(x) = −x^2 − x + 42\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
